-"""FM trained with a sampled within-user softmax ranking loss.
+"""FM trained with a full within-user softmax ranking loss.
 
-This refines the BPR experiment: instead of one positive-vs-one-negative pair,
-each training example is one positive row competing against several negatives
-shown to the same user. Cross-entropy over [positive, sampled negatives] is a
-small listwise/rank-softmax objective and should put more pressure on top-of-list
-separation than independent random pairs.
+This refines sampled softmax by removing negative sampling noise: for each eligible
+user, all of that user's training impressions compete in one softmax and the
+positive set receives the probability mass. The model and features remain the
+same as the FM baseline/BPR variants.
 """
